\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Let A be simple separable unital infinite-dimensional nuclear stably finite with nonempty tracial-state space, and let B be its uniform tracial completion. For any free ultrafilter $\omega $, does real rank zero of the designated uniform tracial ultrapower $B^\omega $ in its quotient C*-norm imply uniform property Gamma for A?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Let A be simple separable unital infinite-dimensional nuclear stably finite with nonempty tracial-state space, and let B be its uniform tracial completion. For any free ultrafilter $\omega $, does real rank zero of the designated uniform tracial ultrapower $B^\omega $ in its quotient C*-norm imply uniform property Gamma for A?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10902v2}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Tracial-projection-methods-and-uniform-property-Gamma-September-23-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

